        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-14T19:07:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe any time the AP resets, the reset of eSPI controller gets handled by this: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/master/chip/it83xx/espi.c#438 i.e. AP reset results in eSPI_RST# assertion which results in interrupt handler getting triggered that ends up calling espi_fw_reset_module().\n\n\u003e We can \u0027t unconditionally do this because we go through this path on sw sync as well, iirc.\n\nThat is correct. espi_fw_reset_module() will have to be done only when the init is not done as part of sysjump. But, check for ESPI_RESET_L condition doesn\u0027t seem necessary.",
